stateDiagram-v2
    [*] --> Unissued
    Unissued --> Issued: channel-specific issuer under Source owner and Ticket root locks
    Issued --> Issued: channel-specific resend replaces generation without extending deadlines or resetting budgets
    Issued --> Cancelled: same original browser and Root reissues candidate / cancel superseded transaction proof
    Issued --> Verified: channel-specific verifier atomically consumes ceremony OTP
    Verified --> Verified: exact input and original binding retry before fixed result deadline
    Verified --> Verified: channel-specific finalizer commits Source binding and audit then Ticket receipt
    Issued --> Unavailable: original deadline reached or owner/root/candidate unavailable (derived refusal)
    Verified --> Unavailable: result deadline reached or owner/root/candidate unavailable (derived refusal)
    Cancelled --> [*]

    note right of Issued
        APP/COM/ORG Email and Telephone registration routes use independent ceremony-owned random keyed proof.
        APP/COM/ORG management-create callers enter their realm-local registration ceremony.
        Complete legacy Source-proof retirement remains acceptance work.
        Original Contact ceremony UUID, Base browser digest, root, owner,
        candidate, destination and generation are immutable issuance bindings.
        Proof deadline is min(verification plus 60 seconds, original Ticket expiry).
        Delivery rechecks original Source and Ticket bindings under locks.
        Email HTTP callers store the original child UUID in a surface-local session.
        Source binding uses its named model transition after typed proof validation.
        APP email HTTP resend retains the original flow and refuses verified proof.
        First-email bootstrap uses its explicit original parent, Session and admission binding.
        Source commits before bootstrap and Contact receipts; no freshness is granted.
        Email delivery, verification and resend reject invalid original bootstrap authority.
        New issuance cancels only prior unconsumed challenges for the same actor, candidate,
        original Root and browser; foreign-browser challenges remain independent.
        APP/COM Email HTTP receipt-fault journeys preserve Source facts and original authority.
        Finalization preserves this proof; receipt reconciliation requires
        the original effective binding and Source audit operation.
        No stored status is inferred from this derived challenge axis.
